            <div class="tip-card">
                <div class="tip-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-car-battery"></i>
                </div>
                <h4>Test Battery Annually</h4>
                <p>Have your battery tested at least once per year, especially before summer and winter when temperature extremes stress batteries.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="tip-card">
                <div class="tip-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-broom"></i>
                </div>
                <h4>Keep Terminals Clean</h4>
                <p>Clean battery terminals and cables regularly. Corrosion prevents proper electrical flow and can cause starting problems.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="tip-card">
                <div class="tip-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-power-off"></i>
                </div>
                <h4>Turn Off Accessories</h4>
                <p>Turn off lights, radio, and other accessories before shutting off your engine to reduce strain on the electrical system.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="tip-card">
                <div class="tip-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>
                </div>
                <h4>Address Warning Lights</h4>
                <p>Don't ignore battery or electrical warning lights. Early diagnosis prevents more expensive repairs and breakdowns.</p>
            </div>

        </div>
